<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kennyo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1543">1543</a>–<a href="/years/1592">1592</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Kennyo Kosa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kennyo was the eleventh head priest of the Hongan-ji, the main temple of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodo-shinshu">Jodo Shinshu</a> Buddhist school, from 1554. From the fortified temple of Ishiyama Hongan-ji in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka">Osaka</a> he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikko-ikki">Ikko-ikki</a> leagues in a long war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> from 1570. He surrendered the temple in 1580, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> later gave him land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, where the Hongan-ji was re-established.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kennyo.jpg" alt="Kennyo" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ブレイズマン · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kennyo02.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
